  "answer": "The KX-100 can't do this measurement, so we won't be setting it up for the 40 GHz qualification. There are two problems. First, the meter only covers 10 MHz to 18 GHz: it refuses SENS:FREQ 40 GHZ with error -222, and it has no calibration factor above 18 GHz, so it can't give a calibrated reading at 40 GHz. Second, its resolution is 0.01 dB (FETC? returns two decimals), so 0.001 dB readings aren't available, and averaging doesn't change that. You'll need a power meter and sensor rated to at least 40 GHz with 0.001 dB resolution.",
  "quote": "A reading finer than the resolution is not available from the instrument, and a signal outside the frequency range cannot be measured with a calibrated result."
}

